Test case with modified current dependent potential (alpha=2.0) in TDOFDFT

The stress reference uses the same order-10 B-spline structure factors as the
Ewald energy. Replacing the former per-atom reciprocal stress changes the final
totalstressref fingerprint from 181323.302533 to 181323.286697 kbar; this
fingerprint sums the absolute values of all nine stress components.
At the final MD configuration, the largest Ewald component change is
0.00263860 kbar. All six components agree with central energy-strain differences
at steps 3e-5 and 1e-5 to within 4.5e-6 kbar. Restoring only the former Ewald
stress in a comparison executable passes the original reference. The energy,
force, MD input, and stress tolerance (0.01 kbar) are unchanged.
